WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.040
This is the shop's Bay,

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.520
named after your shop,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.560
so here it's Ridgeline Auto Repair Bay.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.440
Under the name,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.080
you can see how many cars are in

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.100
the shop, and how many updates went out

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.780
today. Every car sits in a column for

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.000
its stage, from checked in to ready for

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.560
pickup. The colored mark on each card shows

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.160
how long the car has been in the

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.120
shop, and you can pick the colors and

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.980
the days in Settings.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.260
An urgency tag,

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.820
low, medium, or high,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.575
flags a customer who needs their car back fast.

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:32.395
Looking for one car?

00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:33.915
Type in the search box.

00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:35.695
A name, a phone number,

00:00:35.695 --> 00:00:38.215
a plate, or a repair order number all

00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:41.175
work, and the Bay filters as you type.

00:00:41.175 --> 00:00:42.235
Or tap a filter,

00:00:42.235 --> 00:00:43.535
like Awaiting approval,

00:00:43.535 --> 00:00:45.115
to see only the cars waiting on a

00:00:45.115 --> 00:00:47.655
customer. Tap any stage heading to open that

00:00:47.655 --> 00:00:48.935
column, and sort it,

00:00:48.935 --> 00:00:51.175
for example most urgent first.

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:52.115
On a phone,

00:00:52.115 --> 00:00:53.695
the Bay becomes a simple list,

00:00:53.695 --> 00:00:55.515
and the tabs move to a bar along

00:00:55.515 --> 00:00:57.115
the bottom, with Settings,

00:00:57.115 --> 00:01:00.089
Plan, Help, and Training under More.

00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:02.849
Customers can also book online,

00:01:02.849 --> 00:01:04.469
on every plan.

00:01:04.469 --> 00:01:06.329
Put your booking link on your website or

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:07.649
your Google profile,

00:01:07.649 --> 00:01:09.749
and their requests show up right here,

00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:11.869
at the top of your Bay.

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:12.889
Tap confirm a time,

00:01:12.889 --> 00:01:14.689
and the car is added with their details

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:15.629
filled in.

00:01:15.629 --> 00:01:18.089
The week's appointments are listed just above.

00:01:18.089 --> 00:01:20.229
Set your appointment hours in Settings,

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:22.849
and customers pick an open time themselves.

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.929
The day before,

00:01:23.929 --> 00:01:25.662
Talk Shops can text them a reminder.

00:01:25.962 --> 00:01:27.762
Let's check in a new car.

00:01:27.762 --> 00:01:32.292
Sam Ortiz just dropped off his 2014 Mazda CX-5.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.172
We enter his name, and choose how to notify him:

00:01:35.172 --> 00:01:37.602
by text, by email, or both.

00:01:37.602 --> 00:01:39.402
Sam wants both.

00:01:39.402 --> 00:01:41.502
Then his cell number and email,

00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:43.842
the vehicle, and what he's hearing:

00:01:43.842 --> 00:01:46.632
a squealing belt on cold starts.

00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:50.502
This box confirms Sam agreed to receive updates.

00:01:50.502 --> 00:01:52.706
Then we check him in.

00:01:53.006 --> 00:01:53.906
And that's it.

00:01:53.906 --> 00:01:56.396
Sam was just notified that we have his car,

00:01:56.396 --> 00:01:58.046
with a link to follow along.

00:01:58.046 --> 00:02:00.176
That link is his own page for this car.

00:02:00.176 --> 00:02:02.366
No app, and no password.

00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:05.246
Every notification shows up here in the message thread,

00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:08.276
marked text or email, so the whole team can see what

00:02:08.276 --> 00:02:09.943
was sent and when.

00:02:10.243 --> 00:02:13.703
Now let's look at a car that's further along.

00:02:13.703 --> 00:02:16.163
Lena's Chevy Malibu came in with the AC

00:02:16.163 --> 00:02:17.443
blowing warm.

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:18.943
The tech found the problem,

00:02:18.943 --> 00:02:20.863
so we'll build an estimate.

00:02:20.863 --> 00:02:21.943
As we type,

00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:24.843
Talk Shops suggests items the shop has saved,

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:26.023
with their prices.

00:02:26.023 --> 00:02:27.403
We pick the AC recharge,

00:02:27.403 --> 00:02:29.543
for 189 dollars.

00:02:29.543 --> 00:02:30.543
Then the condenser,

00:02:30.543 --> 00:02:32.603
for 624.

00:02:32.603 --> 00:02:34.783
Anything new can be saved for next time

00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:36.084
with one checkbox.

00:02:36.384 --> 00:02:38.024
When the estimate is ready,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.784
we send it for approval.

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:41.724
Talk Shops writes the message for you,

00:02:41.724 --> 00:02:43.784
with the total and the customer's link.

00:02:43.784 --> 00:02:45.904
You can change the wording if you like.

00:02:45.904 --> 00:02:47.040
Then we send it.

00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:48.166
No problem.

00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:50.766
Here's what Lena sees when she opens the link on her

00:02:50.766 --> 00:02:51.456
phone.

00:02:51.456 --> 00:02:53.466
Her car, where it's at in the process,

00:02:53.466 --> 00:02:54.426
and the estimate.

00:02:54.426 --> 00:02:57.576
She can approve or decline each repair on its own.

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.646
Let's say she approves the recharge,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.836
but holds off on the condenser for now.

00:03:01.836 --> 00:03:03.576
She types her name to sign,

00:03:03.576 --> 00:03:05.046
and sends her decision.

00:03:05.046 --> 00:03:08.376
And every customer page links to the privacy policy at the

00:03:08.376 --> 00:03:09.738
bottom.

00:03:10.838 --> 00:03:13.928
Back at the shop, her answer shows up right away.

00:03:13.928 --> 00:03:16.118
You can see exactly what she approved,

00:03:16.118 --> 00:03:17.990
and her signature with the time.

00:03:18.401 --> 00:03:21.911
From here, you move the car along as the work happens.

00:03:21.911 --> 00:03:23.021
In progress.

00:03:23.021 --> 00:03:24.311
Quality check.

00:03:24.311 --> 00:03:26.231
Each step can notify the customer,

00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:28.151
and you decide which ones go out.

00:03:28.151 --> 00:03:30.791
And when it's done, ready for pickup.

00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:34.961
The customer is notified with the total and your hours.
